{"added":{"value":"2026-09-24"},"brand":{"value":"Dayton Audio"},"curves":{"frequency_response":{"origin":"manufacturer_product_page","value":{"data_format":"frd","local_path":"response_data/response.frd","type":"FILE"}},"impedance":{"origin":"manufacturer_product_page","value":{"data_format":"zma","local_path":"response_data/response.zma","type":"FILE"}}},"data_sources":{"value":{"manufacturer_datasheet":"https://daytonaudio.com/images/resources/295-672--dayton-audio-pcs10-4-specification-sheet.pdf","manufacturer_product_page":"https://daytonaudio.com/product/2206/pcs10-4-10-paper-cone-subwoofer-driver-4-ohm"}},"description":{"value":"The Dayton Audio PCS10-4 is a 10\" 4Ω paper cone subwoofer driver built for subwoofer projects and multi-way speaker systems that need deep low-frequency output without a premium price. Its grey poly-coated paper cone, matching inverted dust cap, large-roll rubber surround, and low-profile stamped steel frame give it a clean, modern look while keeping installation practical. With a 33 Hz Fs, 5.6 mm Xmax, 88.8 dB sensitivity, and 150 watts RMS power handling, the PCS10-4 offers a strong balance of extension, output, and value, while also serving as a drop-in replacement woofer for the Dayton Audio CS1000 powered subwoofer. Product Highlights 10\" cone area and 33 Hz Fs help deliver deeper bass from compact to medium enclosures Grey poly-coated paper cone provides classic bass performance with a modern finished look 11.2 mm peak-to-peak excursion delivers ample displacement for high output capability Vented motor, former, and spider area help improve cooling during extended playback Shallow flange stamped steel frame helps create a clean, low-profile installation 150 watts RMS power handling is a great match for moderately sized subwoofer amplifiers 4Ω impedance makes it a practical match for many powered subwoofer amplifiers"},"driver_type":{"value":["woofer","subwoofer"]},"manufacturer":{"value":"Dayton Audio"},"model":{"value":"PCS10